VI. Foundational Theory: Hybrid Systems and Contact Dynamics

Sanfelice, R. G. (2022). Hybrid Feedback Control. Princeton University Press.

Comprehensive treatment of hybrid dynamical systems, including jump maps, reset laws, and stability theory. The measure-valued hybrid dynamics (Definition 2.1) and the reset map formulation follow this framework.

Papamichalis, M., & Ruane, R. (2026). Support-Safe Variational Hybrid Filtering for Contact-Mode and Sparse-Law Recovery. arXiv preprint arXiv:2605.16398. (See Section I.)

Establishes that contact-rich robot dynamics are hybrid: a single observation can match several latent states and contact regimes (free, impact, stick–slip) . The branch-loss failure mode—where a standard amortized filter permanently loses a feasible contact transition—is formally identified and addressed through the support-safe proposal.

Aubin, J.-P., & Cellina, A. (1984). Differential Inclusions: Set-Valued Maps and Viability Theory. Springer.

Provides the mathematical foundations for differential inclusions and nonsmooth dynamical systems, including the measure-valued evolution of state distributions under reset maps.

