VII. Surveys and Reviews

Han, L., & Wang, H. (2026). Robotic manipulation of deformable objects: a comprehensive review. Robotic Intelligence and Automation, 212–227. DOI: 10.1108/RIA-06-2025-0168 

A comprehensive review of modelling, sensing, planning, and control of deformable-object manipulation. Identifies that multi-modal perception fused with learning-augmented physics models is improving state estimation , and addresses critical knowledge gaps including real-time state estimation under partial observability.

Caporali, A., Cuiral-Zueco, I., López-Nicolás, G., & Palli, G. (2026). Robotic perception and manipulation of deformable linear objects: A survey. The International Journal of Robotics Research, Early Access, 1–44. DOI: 10.1177/02783649261432253 

A survey of state-of-the-art methods for deformable linear objects, covering physical and data-driven modeling techniques, simulation environments, and estimation strategies . Concludes with a critical discussion of current limitations and promising directions for future research.

Caporali, A., et al. (2026). A survey on robotic manipulation of deformable objects: Recent advances and new research directions. Neurocomputing. 

Identifies real-time state estimation under partial observability as a top open challenge for deformable object manipulation.

Wu, C., et al. (2024). When Vision Meets Touch: A Contemporary Review for Visuotactile Sensors From the Signal Processing Perspective. Semantic Scholar. 

A comprehensive review of visuotactile sensors from the signal processing perspective, with an outlook on future research directions . Provides context for the multimodal encoder design.

