VIII. Datasets and Benchmarks

SoftVTBench (2026). A Deformation-Aware Visuo-Tactile Dataset and Benchmark for Deformable-Object Manipulation. arXiv preprint arXiv:2608.18701. 

A visuo-tactile dataset for learning and evaluating contact-rich deformable-object manipulation. Contains 4,000 expert demonstrations across 40 pick-and-place tasks, with more than 50 assets including volumetric deformable objects and visually matched rigid twins . Provides synchronized multi-view RGB observations, RGB tactile sensing with marker motion, proprioception, and language instructions .

Limitation relative to AHLF. SoftVTBench provides 4,000 demonstrations, but they are not labeled by contact stratum at transition level. The analytical calibration requirement for stratified conformal coverage (Lemma 16.3, Corollary D.4.1) is n_s \geq 8{,}628 per stratum for \epsilon_s = 0.02, |\mathcal{S}| = 5, \delta = 0.05. This exceeds what is currently available without manual annotation, establishing an empirical gap that would need to be addressed in any future experimental validation.

Deform360 (2025). 198 objects, 1,980 interaction sequences, 215+ hours of visuotactile data. Provides a large-scale resource for deformable object manipulation but similarly lacks contact-stratum labels at transition level.

